From: Liminix AX6600 bring-up
Subject: ath11k: pci: keep ASPM disabled for the QCN9074

This board's QCN9074 (IPQ6018 host, RE-CS-02) goes to RDDM during its
QMI handshake whenever the PCIe link has ASPM enabled: the firmware
download completes, the MHI READY transition happens, and then the
device raises MHI_CB_EE_RDDM before it ever reaches mission mode. The
ax6600 branch recorded the same failure and added pcie_aspm=off to the
kernel command line - but that workaround never actually applied here,
because this board's U-Boot web uploader replaces the FIT command line
(/chosen/bootargs is in the image, cat /proc/cmdline shows only
console=). It cannot be fixed from the command line at all.

ath11k already has the right hook: ath11k_pci_power_up() calls
ath11k_pci_aspm_disable() before starting MHI, deliberately, because the
switch to AMSS state is known to be ASPM-sensitive. The link state is
only put back in two places, and for the QCN9074 neither is wanted:

  - ath11k_pci_start() restores it after the firmware download, i.e.
    exactly in time for the QMI handshake. Keep it disabled there.
  - ath11k_pci_power_down() restores it "in case firmware bootup fails",
    which re-enables ASPM on the way out of a failed probe. Leave it
    alone too, so a failed probe does not hand ASPM back before the
    next one.

Everything else keeps the upstream behaviour, including the existing
single-MSI guard.

Signed-off-by: Liminix AX6600 bring-up <liminix@invalid>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/pci.c
@@ -855,8 +855,17 @@
 {
 	struct ath11k_pci *ab_pci = ath11k_pci_priv(ab);
 
-	/* restore aspm in case firmware bootup fails */
-	ath11k_pci_aspm_restore(ab_pci);
+	/* restore aspm in case firmware bootup fails
+	 *
+	 * Liminix: not for the QCN9074. ath11k_pci_power_up() disables ASPM
+	 * before the firmware download, and this is the only thing that puts
+	 * it back; the card RDDMs during its QMI handshake whenever ASPM is
+	 * enabled, and the usual workaround (pcie_aspm=off) is not available
+	 * because this board's U-Boot replaces the FIT command line. Leaving
+	 * ASPM off is what that option would have done.
+	 */
+	if (ab->hw_rev != ATH11K_HW_QCN9074_HW10)
+		ath11k_pci_aspm_restore(ab_pci);
 
 	ath11k_pci_force_wake(ab_pci->ab);
 
@@ -897,8 +906,16 @@
 
 	/* TODO: for now don't restore ASPM in case of single MSI
 	 * vector as MHI register reading in M2 causes system hang.
+	 *
+	 * Liminix: keep ASPM disabled for the QCN9074 even with multiple MSI
+	 * vectors. ath11k_pci_power_up() has already disabled it for the
+	 * firmware download; restoring it here re-enables it just in time
+	 * for the QMI handshake, which is where this board's QCN9074 RDDMs.
+	 * See ath11k_pci_power_down() for why pcie_aspm=off cannot be used.
 	 */
-	if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_MULTI_MSI_VECTORS, &ab->dev_flags))
+	if (ab->hw_rev == ATH11K_HW_QCN9074_HW10)
+		ath11k_info(ab, "leaving PCI ASPM disabled for QCN9074\n");
+	else if (test_bit(ATH11K_FLAG_MULTI_MSI_VECTORS, &ab->dev_flags))
 		ath11k_pci_aspm_restore(ab_pci);
 	else
 		ath11k_info(ab, "leaving PCI ASPM disabled to avoid MHI M2 problems\n");
